registry.npmjs.org
api.anthropic.com
github.com
api.github.com
codeload.github.com
objects.githubusercontent.com
raw.githubusercontent.com
# The delivered app's own preview URL. The post-deploy acceptance check (Gate C) probes the LIVE
# service from inside this container — SPA HTML, bundle asset, token-aware API calls — so without
# this the check cannot reach the very thing it exists to verify, and every delivery withholds its
# URL. ECS Express hands out `<id>.<region>.on.aws`, which is not known until after the deploy, so
# the pattern has to cover the domain rather than one host.
#
# TRADEOFF, deliberately taken: this also lets build code reach any OTHER Express service in AWS.
# Those are other apps' HTTP endpoints, not credentials, and untrusted customers are still barred
# by the standing Gate B ban. The tight version is Gate B's C1 fence (own SG, deny-by-default,
# per-job rules) — docs/backlog/hardening-2026-08-30/c1-egress-fence.md.
*.on.aws
